{#
  HOMEPAGE — composition only.

  Each section is a partial that owns its own markup; this file decides only
  which ones render and in what order. No content and no styling decisions
  belong here: strings live in src/_data/, colours in styles/tokens.css.

  THE PAGE IS COMPLETE. The v2 blocks that used to follow About Me — the
  3-column panel shell, At a Glance, the Projects carousel, Testimonials, the
  milestone timeline, How I Think, Skills and the old contact footer — were all
  removed in the cleanup sweep, and the two that were coming back have both
  landed: Testimonials, which is now the second half of the About supersection
  rather than a section of its own, and the Footer.

  THERE IS NO NAV CONTRACT ANY MORE. This file used to carry one: the ids
  #summary, #featured-works, #all-about-me and #contact had to appear in that
  document order because scripts/nav.js walked site.nav to highlight the active
  bottom-nav item. That bar and that script are both gone — the header in
  partials/nav.njk is plain anchors with no JS — so section order here is now a
  design decision and nothing else.

  One header anchor still points at nothing: /#contact has no target until the
  Footer is rebuilt. /#featured-works resolves again as of the My Work section
  below, which carries that id.
#}

